      "text": " The initial load proportionality factor, [Formula: (normal(Δ) × (λ)_((i × n)))], is computed as\n\n[Formula: (((normal(Δ) × (λ)_((i × n))) = ((normal(Δ) × (l)_((i × n))))/((l)_((p × e × r × i × o × d)))) ,)]\n\nwhere [Formula: (l)_((p × e × r × i × o × d))] is a user-specified total arc length scale factor (typically set equal to 1). This value of [Formula: (normal(Δ) × (λ)_((i × n)))] is used during the first iteration of a Riks step. For subsequent iterations and increments the value of [Formula: λ] is computed automatically, so you have no control over the load magnitude. The value of [Formula: λ] is part of the solution. Minimum and maximum arc length increments, [Formula: (normal(Δ) × (l)_((m × i × n)))] and [Formula: (normal(Δ) × (l)_((m × a × x)))], can be used to control the automatic incrementation."
